WEBVTT

00:33.616 --> 00:35.618
[footsteps approaching]

00:49.507 --> 00:51.259
These cookies taste better.

00:55.138 --> 00:55.972
Hey,

00:56.931 --> 00:59.100
would you mind telling me
what my symbol is?

01:05.940 --> 01:07.233
[Chishiya inhales]

01:07.317 --> 01:09.235
That guy you hang out with?

01:10.070 --> 01:12.572
You should know that he's a murderer.

01:13.823 --> 01:16.493
- What?
- [Chishiya] His name's Sunato Banda.

01:17.452 --> 01:18.953
It was in the newspaper.

01:19.913 --> 01:23.166
Murdered four women, so,
that makes him a serial killer.

01:23.833 --> 01:26.628
And, you know, that's punishable by death.

01:27.712 --> 01:29.506
That's a filthy lie.

01:29.589 --> 01:30.757
[Chishiya] No. It's true.

01:31.674 --> 01:33.426
Know what I think?

01:33.510 --> 01:35.804
I think he's the Jack of Hearts.

01:36.888 --> 01:37.972
[gasps]

01:38.056 --> 01:39.766
There's only five of us left.

01:40.600 --> 01:42.185
Time is running out,

01:42.268 --> 01:44.687
so the Jack's gonna start
to get aggressive now.

01:46.689 --> 01:48.233
Might as well share symbols.

01:52.987 --> 01:55.949
For the moment, you're in a good position.

01:57.283 --> 01:59.285
The Jack still trusts you.

01:59.828 --> 02:02.622
So if anyone is going to lie to the Jack,

02:02.705 --> 02:03.873
it has to be you.

02:05.125 --> 02:06.167
Which means

02:07.043 --> 02:08.920
this game can only end one way.

02:09.671 --> 02:11.381
The key player here is you.

02:13.133 --> 02:14.759
[draws breath]

02:16.970 --> 02:19.681
I'm sure this is a lot,
and you don't trust me yet.

02:20.557 --> 02:24.018
For what it's worth,
there's no advantage for me to lie,

02:24.102 --> 02:26.312
so I'll tell you the truth
about your symbol.

02:27.063 --> 02:30.108
Don't you wanna make sure
that Banda's telling you the truth?

02:31.651 --> 02:34.904
What makes you think
that I would trust you over him?

02:35.697 --> 02:37.824
[Chishiya]
You don't have to if you don't want to.

02:38.408 --> 02:41.244
If I were in your shoes,
I'd want to weigh my options.

02:42.287 --> 02:44.664
And I've got no reason to lie to you.

02:45.540 --> 02:48.168
Banda's a murderer, and that's a fact.

02:51.045 --> 02:52.881
I still don't trust you.

02:53.464 --> 02:54.424
Fine.

02:54.924 --> 02:58.303
You'll see for yourself,
once the next round is over.

02:59.971 --> 03:01.890
You're a spade, just so you know.

03:06.227 --> 03:08.146
So, will you tell me mine?

03:12.483 --> 03:16.196
Come on. I told you what yours is.

03:17.780 --> 03:19.282
I never agreed to this deal.

03:26.956 --> 03:27.957
Heart.

03:34.130 --> 03:36.132
[lively cello music]

03:42.472 --> 03:43.723
What's happening?

03:51.981 --> 03:53.691
I think the Jack of Hearts is…

03:54.859 --> 03:56.069
is that guy right there.

04:00.240 --> 04:02.075
I thought he was suspicious too.

04:04.160 --> 04:05.453
Well, don't worry.

04:07.121 --> 04:10.083
He'll die this round.
You can trust me on that.

04:12.627 --> 04:14.629
[tense, dramatic music]

04:22.011 --> 04:23.429
[man] That kid Banda.

04:26.140 --> 04:28.726
He's the one we need to watch out for.

04:32.313 --> 04:35.650
You know that emo kid
who lied first to kill that big guy?

04:36.651 --> 04:39.279
Banda's the one
who convinced him to lie to the man.

04:39.362 --> 04:41.781
- I saw him do it.
- Huh?

04:43.825 --> 04:45.368
He whispered in his ear.

04:46.786 --> 04:52.292
Banda looks innocent, but he's got
no actual empathy for anyone else.

04:53.001 --> 04:56.546
He can only process human emotion
through logic and reason.

04:57.380 --> 04:58.631
[sighs]

04:59.465 --> 05:01.676
He's certifiably psychopathic.

05:05.263 --> 05:07.390
He's the Jack of Hearts. I'm sure of it.

05:28.745 --> 05:30.747
[theme music]

06:49.283 --> 06:50.910
[sighs unsteadily]

07:06.092 --> 07:08.052
There are only five of us left,

07:08.761 --> 07:10.930
and unfortunately, my partner's dead.

07:13.808 --> 07:16.310
I asked that guy Matsushita
what my symbol is,

07:16.394 --> 07:18.312
but he told me he doesn't trust me,

07:19.522 --> 07:21.983
and I'm pretty sure that he lied to me.

07:22.066 --> 07:23.609
Sort of a hunch, I guess.

07:25.236 --> 07:29.073
So, would you mind
telling me what my symbol is?

07:29.574 --> 07:31.617
I know this is kind of a big ask.

07:32.869 --> 07:36.873
But if you want, I promise to tell you
your symbol in exchange.

07:37.498 --> 07:39.959
I… don't mean to presume,

07:40.042 --> 07:43.379
but you strike me as an honest person,
at least from over here.

07:44.172 --> 07:46.174
[breathing unsteadily]

07:48.301 --> 07:52.680
Also, that Yaba guy strikes me
as a bit of a conman,

07:53.598 --> 07:56.392
and since you're aligned with him,
I thought you should know.

08:11.282 --> 08:12.950
Let me get right to the point.

08:14.076 --> 08:15.912
Are you the Jack of Hearts or not?

08:17.914 --> 08:19.707
I'll only say this.

08:20.708 --> 08:22.335
I might be the Jack of Hearts,

08:23.169 --> 08:26.255
but the fact that you're bringing it up
means it could be you.

08:27.507 --> 08:28.382
[chuckles]

08:28.466 --> 08:29.509
[zips up]

08:30.927 --> 08:34.055
I know one thing.
You and I will never get along.

08:36.641 --> 08:37.558
[Chishiya] Your symbol

08:38.726 --> 08:39.977
is a heart.

08:41.604 --> 08:43.105
Now, what about mine?

08:44.690 --> 08:46.192
It's a club, right?

08:53.783 --> 08:55.034
[breathing unsteadily]

08:55.618 --> 08:56.911
[running away]

08:56.994 --> 08:58.454
These taste better, you know.

09:46.669 --> 09:50.381
[Chishiya] Five people left,
and only two pairs.

09:50.464 --> 09:52.842
The Jack's definitely going
to make a move this round.

09:52.925 --> 09:53.968
[Matsushita] Yeah…

10:00.766 --> 10:01.934
[chuckles]

10:03.686 --> 10:07.732
I guess that this is the last round.

10:17.450 --> 10:19.035
[breathing shakily]

10:25.625 --> 10:26.584
[Yaba] Heart.

10:33.716 --> 10:35.426
Thank you very much.

10:47.229 --> 10:48.356
Diamond.

10:59.742 --> 11:00.868
Spade.

11:12.296 --> 11:14.298
All right, and now it's my turn.

11:19.387 --> 11:20.471
Spade.

11:24.016 --> 11:26.102
[computer over PA] It is time to answer.

11:26.727 --> 11:30.773
Please enter a solitary confinement
cell of your choosing.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.987
[creaking]

11:37.071 --> 11:38.531
- [slam echoing]
- [lock clicks]

11:44.161 --> 11:46.330
I bet Matsushita lied to me.

11:46.414 --> 11:47.790
I'm sure he did.

11:48.916 --> 11:52.128
And Kotoko, she totally ignored me.

11:53.629 --> 11:56.924
Meaning that… it's a diamond,

11:57.007 --> 11:58.801
or a spade, right?

12:00.636 --> 12:02.304
[sighs] Hmm.

12:02.388 --> 12:04.223
Ah, well…

12:05.641 --> 12:07.143
I'll go with my gut.

12:07.810 --> 12:09.812
[tense, dramatic music]

12:25.119 --> 12:27.246
[computer] Please give your answer.

12:32.209 --> 12:34.211
[explosion echoing]

13:15.169 --> 13:16.712
I won.

13:18.547 --> 13:19.799
Huh! [laughs]

13:31.519 --> 13:33.312
[door opens]

13:37.942 --> 13:40.861
I had a feeling
you were the Jack of Hearts.

13:43.906 --> 13:44.740
But how did you…

13:44.824 --> 13:46.700
You teamed up with Banda from the start,

13:46.784 --> 13:49.203
and he's a murderer,
so it just made sense.

13:50.329 --> 13:51.872
We should be a team.

13:55.376 --> 13:56.502
[Chishiya] Even if somehow,

13:57.086 --> 13:59.588
you were moved
by Banda's little monologue,

13:59.672 --> 14:01.549
I knew you wouldn't trust him.

14:01.632 --> 14:04.927
You don't trust strangers.
And certainly not as fast as that.

14:05.845 --> 14:07.346
[door opens]

14:07.429 --> 14:10.057
[Banda] Most people
won't even talk to a guy like me.

14:10.140 --> 14:11.934
But you wanted to kill me.

14:14.478 --> 14:17.022
I could sense that in you right away.

14:17.106 --> 14:20.484
So I wanted to see if you were smart,
or just stupid,

14:20.568 --> 14:22.528
or whether you were a true psychopath.

14:23.821 --> 14:24.697
You mean…

14:25.614 --> 14:28.325
You thought you were controlling me
this whole time.

14:29.910 --> 14:32.621
But I was manipulating you
into thinking that way.

14:33.664 --> 14:38.586
Ultimately, it was your huge
superiority complex that gave you away.

14:39.503 --> 14:42.590
[Chishiya] That kind of self-importance
usually comes

14:42.673 --> 14:44.592
from being put in a special position.

14:44.675 --> 14:46.760
Something that made you feel untouchable.

14:46.844 --> 14:49.221
Like being chosen as the Jack.

14:49.305 --> 14:51.265
You guys are wrong about this.

14:51.348 --> 14:54.768
- Banda is the Jack of Hearts!
- [Yaba] Sorry, kid.

14:59.607 --> 15:00.900
It's not Banda.

15:11.535 --> 15:13.579
You and Kotoko were connected.

15:14.580 --> 15:16.999
I told Kotoko what her symbol was.

15:18.626 --> 15:20.169
And yet, she still died.

15:23.255 --> 15:28.510
Which means Kotoko was being manipulated
by someone other than me.

15:30.387 --> 15:31.764
Well, then,

15:32.556 --> 15:34.683
you should be accusing this guy instead.

15:34.767 --> 15:36.810
Every time I went to the cafeteria,

15:37.478 --> 15:41.941
you and Kotoko would always be there,
getting snacks at the same time.

15:42.024 --> 15:44.109
[woman 1] This break
couldn't come soon enough.

15:44.193 --> 15:46.195
- [man 1] I don't…
- [woman 1] I'm scared. Aren't you?

15:46.278 --> 15:48.948
- [man 2] When you trust…
- [woman 1] I don't know what's going on.

15:49.031 --> 15:51.033
I don't know if I can keep doing this.

15:51.116 --> 15:52.576
[woman 2] You can trust me.

15:52.660 --> 15:55.412
[woman 1] Every time I get through it,
I think, "I made it."

15:56.163 --> 15:57.581
[Chishiya] And each time,

15:58.624 --> 16:00.960
you'd get the exact same kind of snack.

16:08.550 --> 16:12.596
You and Kotoko were secretly
communicating in the cafeteria.

16:12.680 --> 16:13.639
Spade.

16:15.516 --> 16:19.770
Both of you were just pretending
that you were being controlled.

16:27.736 --> 16:30.656
There were four different flavors
of the snack.

16:32.116 --> 16:35.369
You would confirm your symbols
by checking the packaging,

16:36.036 --> 16:38.622
using those snacks
as a code with each other.

16:38.706 --> 16:40.290
I caught on pretty quickly.

16:56.640 --> 16:57.933
[Yaba] And then,

16:58.600 --> 17:01.437
you told Kotoko
to give me the wrong symbol.

17:02.396 --> 17:03.522
Diamond.

17:06.692 --> 17:08.861
[Yaba] I really did trust her.

17:11.321 --> 17:12.698
Except at the end.

17:14.241 --> 17:15.576
[gasps]

17:15.659 --> 17:17.870
When did the three of you guys
start working together?

17:18.454 --> 17:21.081
Well, the very first announcement said

17:21.165 --> 17:24.209
that this game is about
how much we can trust one another.

17:25.335 --> 17:27.337
So we simply followed that principle.

17:29.757 --> 17:32.551
In order to gain someone's trust,
you can't

17:33.427 --> 17:36.764
control, or manipulate,
or guide them in any way.

17:37.431 --> 17:40.517
You can't brainwash or hypnotize them,

17:40.601 --> 17:42.811
lie to them or instill fear.

17:45.898 --> 17:47.357
It's called equality.

17:54.656 --> 17:55.949
I know one thing.

17:56.033 --> 17:57.910
You and I will never get along.

17:58.786 --> 17:59.870
[Banda] Tell me.

18:01.663 --> 18:02.873
I want to know

18:03.916 --> 18:06.752
why you're here
playing the games in this country?

18:10.506 --> 18:12.800
I'll tell you why I'm here.

18:12.883 --> 18:15.677
I've never seen a place
more beautiful than this one.

18:19.598 --> 18:21.183
I'm here because I…

18:21.850 --> 18:25.813
because I believe that this world
is a place that is worth conquering.

18:29.358 --> 18:32.694
Well, then, you and I might be
more alike than you think.

18:37.032 --> 18:39.409
[Yaba] I'm starting
to get that feeling too.

18:40.828 --> 18:43.372
Trust is the most important thing
in this game.

18:46.583 --> 18:48.752
We'll be good for each other.

18:48.836 --> 18:52.297
Intellectual equals,
and trustworthy partners.

18:58.887 --> 19:01.723
Wait a sec.
What makes you so sure it's me?

19:01.807 --> 19:04.476
The Jack of Hearts
could easily be one of you guys.

19:04.560 --> 19:08.397
Okay, maybe I did try to blame everything
on you by setting you up, but look!

19:08.480 --> 19:09.857
But that's not enough, huh?

19:09.940 --> 19:13.068
You guys don't have any proof
that I'm the Jack of Hearts, huh?

19:13.569 --> 19:15.612
- [Chishiya] You sure about that?
- Huh?

19:16.405 --> 19:18.073
Just think about it.

19:18.157 --> 19:22.828
If they suspected that you were the Jack,
then why did you survive this last round?

19:23.537 --> 19:26.540
Why didn't Banda lie?
Tell you the wrong thing?

19:26.623 --> 19:29.501
The reason you're still alive
is because you're the Jack.

19:34.923 --> 19:37.050
And these guys planned to keep you alive

19:38.177 --> 19:41.346
because they decided they wanna
get information out of you.

19:42.222 --> 19:43.640
[footsteps]

19:51.440 --> 19:53.358
[breathing shakily]

19:54.860 --> 19:58.488
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Round 14, start.

20:00.490 --> 20:01.450
[grunts]

20:02.743 --> 20:03.744
What are you doing?

20:03.827 --> 20:05.662
[panting]

20:05.746 --> 20:07.748
There have been so few opportunities

20:07.831 --> 20:10.500
to really get to talk
to the citizens of this place.

20:10.584 --> 20:13.545
We need you to tell us
the ins and outs of this country.

20:15.422 --> 20:17.299
[gasping]

20:18.258 --> 20:21.803
[Banda] I'm sorry that
we won't be able to kill you, but…

20:24.473 --> 20:26.683
there are a lot of other ways to have fun.

20:27.935 --> 20:29.436
[whimpering]

20:33.690 --> 20:35.692
[screams]

20:38.862 --> 20:40.864
[low rumbling]

20:54.253 --> 20:55.545
[sighs]

21:20.445 --> 21:22.406
[Yaba] We didn't get very much out of him.

21:23.615 --> 21:26.994
[Banda] I can't believe he just gave up
like that and said the wrong answer,

21:27.786 --> 21:30.664
even though we told him
what the real answer was.

21:32.374 --> 21:35.043
He certainly gave up
faster than I expected.

21:35.127 --> 21:36.545
Hmm. Yeah.

21:48.473 --> 21:49.474
[projector whirring]

21:49.558 --> 21:51.351
My name is Kaito Kameyama.

21:52.060 --> 21:53.854
- [woman] Fireworks…
- [Ann] I'll try to get out.

21:53.937 --> 21:54.980
[yelling]

21:55.063 --> 21:56.606
[man 1] It's lots of fun here.

21:57.316 --> 22:01.403
There are no laws,
so we can loot and kill as we please.

22:02.446 --> 22:03.697
When I play the games,

22:04.197 --> 22:06.074
It's like,"I don't fuckin' care!"

22:06.158 --> 22:07.200
Total freedom. Oh yeah!

22:07.284 --> 22:08.493
[mumbling]

22:08.577 --> 22:09.995
It feels pretty great.

22:11.872 --> 22:13.290
I hate it here.

22:13.874 --> 22:16.793
That's why I'm smoking weed…

22:16.877 --> 22:20.380
[giggling] …and just flipping out!

22:23.342 --> 22:24.968
[Kaito] What is this world?

22:26.470 --> 22:28.096
What are these games?

22:28.889 --> 22:30.640
Who's behind all of this?

22:31.391 --> 22:33.393
- [gasping]
- [man 2] You guys are fucking crazy.

22:33.477 --> 22:34.644
I'm gonna kill you!

22:34.728 --> 22:35.854
[yells]

22:35.937 --> 22:38.690
Hey! Stop filming and help me here!

22:38.774 --> 22:40.484
- [gasping]
- It's okay!

22:40.567 --> 22:41.860
What the fuck are you doing?

22:42.652 --> 22:44.821
- Come here! I'm gonna kill you!
- Wait! Don't--

22:44.905 --> 22:46.198
- I'm gonna--
- Hey! Don't!

22:52.162 --> 22:54.498
[Kaito] Life is totally meaningless here.

22:58.585 --> 23:00.462
Human beings are worthless.

23:02.547 --> 23:04.925
Is that what this world
is trying to tell us?

23:30.117 --> 23:32.035
Arisu. Do it.

23:32.119 --> 23:33.745
[Arisu] Do we go back where we came from?

23:33.829 --> 23:35.580
[Tatta] Otherwise everyone will die!

23:40.836 --> 23:42.838
[wind whistling]

23:54.141 --> 23:54.975
[Kuina] There.

23:55.684 --> 23:56.643
Thank you.

24:03.024 --> 24:04.109
[Arisu] You know…

24:07.404 --> 24:10.031
when Kyuma and I were talking
at the end of the game,

24:11.992 --> 24:13.452
I figured something out.

24:16.163 --> 24:18.248
They were all players to begin with,

24:19.749 --> 24:21.126
and then eventually,

24:22.335 --> 24:24.546
they started making the games themselves.

24:29.217 --> 24:30.469
I mean that…

24:32.637 --> 24:34.264
we might not be able

24:35.182 --> 24:36.600
to ever get home…

24:39.144 --> 24:41.521
even if we beat every single game.

24:45.066 --> 24:46.276
Because…

24:48.612 --> 24:51.406
our world might not even exist anymore.

24:54.659 --> 24:55.785
Which means that…

24:57.829 --> 24:59.664
Tatta sacrificed himself

25:01.082 --> 25:02.459
for nothing.

25:03.710 --> 25:05.212
[breathing shakily]

25:13.136 --> 25:14.846
[sobbing]

25:17.265 --> 25:18.975
That might not be true.

25:20.810 --> 25:23.355
There might still be a way to get back.

25:24.314 --> 25:25.899
I'll keep trying.

25:27.234 --> 25:29.152
I'll keep playing the games.

25:31.863 --> 25:33.740
Tatta won't have died in vain.

25:43.291 --> 25:45.293
[birdsong]

25:46.670 --> 25:48.255
[Usagi] Are you really going?

25:48.964 --> 25:51.174
[Kuina] I'm worried
about Ann and Chishiya.

25:52.008 --> 25:53.510
I'm gonna go look for them.

25:55.679 --> 25:59.307
We need more friends if we're gonna
take down the King of Spades.

26:00.392 --> 26:02.185
And the more games that we beat,

26:03.103 --> 26:05.105
the closer we'll be to our goal.

26:07.023 --> 26:08.066
[sighs]

26:08.149 --> 26:09.484
Don't worry.

26:09.568 --> 26:11.444
We'll see each other again.

26:13.113 --> 26:14.114
Usagi.

26:15.365 --> 26:16.908
You need to rest.

26:19.619 --> 26:22.581
Arisu. Take care of Usagi.

26:24.207 --> 26:26.459
[wind whistling]

26:26.543 --> 26:28.670
Well, be safe.

27:07.417 --> 27:09.419
[papers fluttering]

27:20.722 --> 27:21.806
[Arisu] You know,

27:22.599 --> 27:24.976
I'd be down with going
to a deserted island.

27:25.060 --> 27:27.062
[lively buzz of voices]

27:28.438 --> 27:30.899
I'd be down with zombies
showing up in Shibuya.

27:30.982 --> 27:33.860
Everyone here gets bitten,
and they all turn into zombies!

27:33.943 --> 27:36.446
- [chuckles]
- Stop it with the zombie talk, will ya?

27:36.529 --> 27:39.658
If zombies did show up here,
only Karube would survive.

27:39.741 --> 27:42.035
- You'd knock 'em out with one punch.
- [chuckles]

27:42.118 --> 27:43.453
I doubt that.

27:43.536 --> 27:45.538
You'd be the one to survive, Arisu.

27:45.622 --> 27:46.956
Me? Why's that?

27:48.541 --> 27:50.585
Because I know you'd outsmart 'em.

27:55.590 --> 27:57.592
[sniffles]

28:02.347 --> 28:03.223
[Karube] What?

28:04.641 --> 28:06.851
Why are you acting like your life is over?

28:07.936 --> 28:08.937
Huh?

28:10.105 --> 28:12.941
Why are you making that face?
You look like it's the end of the world.

28:13.983 --> 28:16.403
I was wondering what was on your mind.
[chuckles]

28:16.945 --> 28:19.155
So fuckin' stupid. [laughs]

28:20.407 --> 28:21.658
Is your life so pathetic

28:21.741 --> 28:24.202
that getting a job
will be the end of the world for you?

28:24.285 --> 28:25.537
[Chota] Don't worry so much.

28:25.620 --> 28:27.247
Use your dad's connections.

28:27.330 --> 28:30.834
Just do whatever you have to do
and leave the deep thoughts for later.

28:31.835 --> 28:32.669
Arisu,

28:33.628 --> 28:36.881
sometimes life
seems like it's at a dead end,

28:36.965 --> 28:40.760
but there's always another path
you can take, even when things go wrong.

28:42.178 --> 28:43.847
- Huh?
- [Chota laughs]

28:46.224 --> 28:50.478
Not really convincing coming from
a part-time bartender, though.

28:50.562 --> 28:53.064
[Karube] Do you have anything smart
to add? I highly doubt it.

28:53.148 --> 28:54.858
[Chota] Let me see…

28:55.608 --> 28:57.777
- See, you got nothin'.
- [laughs]

28:57.861 --> 29:00.447
- What you said was still really cool.
- Shut up.

29:00.530 --> 29:03.533
- [Chota] Hard to do on the spot.
- [Karube] Don't give me your shit.

29:03.616 --> 29:06.578
- [Chota laughing] See?
- [Karube] Keep your mouth shut, then.

29:28.266 --> 29:29.476
[panting]

29:42.655 --> 29:43.531
Oh.

29:46.367 --> 29:47.452
Mugwort.

30:15.146 --> 30:16.231
[Usagi sighs]

30:16.314 --> 30:18.191
Hey, do you wanna come hunting?

30:19.901 --> 30:22.070
We don't have any food left.

30:23.696 --> 30:25.198
I managed to pick this,

30:25.990 --> 30:27.992
but we won't survive on plants alone.

30:35.458 --> 30:36.668
[sighs]

30:38.294 --> 30:39.295
Hey!

30:41.089 --> 30:43.967
If you wanna eat meat,
then you need to help.

30:58.022 --> 30:59.607
[birdsong]

31:06.197 --> 31:07.574
[whispers] Arisu! Get it!

31:23.923 --> 31:25.091
[Arisu groans]

31:26.759 --> 31:27.802
[sighs]

31:29.804 --> 31:32.223
Arisu, would you get serious about this?

31:33.349 --> 31:34.309
[sighs]

31:34.851 --> 31:36.519
We don't have food for tonight.

31:44.527 --> 31:47.030
[gasps] Arisu, look! Over there!

31:52.493 --> 31:53.369
Ah!

32:00.126 --> 32:01.294
It's there! Look, look!

32:03.296 --> 32:04.464
[thud]

32:07.383 --> 32:08.760
Ah! Aah!

32:09.260 --> 32:10.136
Uh…

32:11.888 --> 32:13.181
Oh, there's one.

32:19.979 --> 32:21.439
[grunts]

32:21.522 --> 32:24.150
- [groans]
- [Usagi] Ah, you were so close!

32:24.233 --> 32:26.361
You're terrible at this, you know?

32:27.779 --> 32:28.947
[Arisu grunts]

32:29.822 --> 32:31.950
Shit. [panting]

32:32.450 --> 32:33.326
Huh.

32:35.495 --> 32:37.205
- [Usagi gasps] What?
- [Arisu] Over there!

32:37.288 --> 32:38.665
- [grunts]
- [Usagi] This way? Oh!

32:39.374 --> 32:40.792
- Usagi, it's there!
- Huh?

32:42.085 --> 32:43.086
Ah!

32:43.711 --> 32:44.712
- Arisu!
- [grunts]

32:45.296 --> 32:46.339
[Usagi] Oh, shoot!

32:46.923 --> 32:49.175
- [whispers] Arisu, there it is.
- [panting]

32:55.223 --> 32:56.265
- [thud]
- [Usagi] Ah!

32:56.349 --> 32:58.142
[Arisu] Oh, man. I give up.

32:59.310 --> 33:00.895
[sighs] Damn it.

33:01.562 --> 33:03.106
No meat for you, I guess, huh?

33:04.399 --> 33:05.942
Oh, I'm starving.

33:07.193 --> 33:08.236
[laughs]

33:10.113 --> 33:11.406
[both laughing]

33:13.658 --> 33:14.867
Come on.

33:20.540 --> 33:21.958
[both sigh]

33:25.294 --> 33:26.587
[clanking]

33:48.359 --> 33:49.861
[Usagi gasps]

34:27.690 --> 34:29.692
[metal creaking]

34:29.776 --> 34:31.444
[rattling]

34:35.448 --> 34:36.574
[Usagi gasps]

35:01.140 --> 35:02.308
[Usagi gasps]

35:03.643 --> 35:04.852
[Arisu] Are you okay?

35:09.148 --> 35:10.441
Film…

35:11.442 --> 35:13.277
- Huh?
- What film?

35:20.827 --> 35:22.161
[Usagi gasps]

35:31.879 --> 35:33.965
[gasps] In here?

35:41.681 --> 35:43.766
[rustling]

35:43.850 --> 35:45.476
[dripping]

35:58.781 --> 36:00.867
[Arisu] He must have been a photographer.

36:06.664 --> 36:08.249
This is eight millimeter film.

36:11.127 --> 36:12.670
Do you watch it with this?

36:54.420 --> 36:56.088
My name is Kaito Kameyama.

36:57.048 --> 36:59.675
For some reason,
electronic devices don't work here.

37:00.635 --> 37:04.430
So I'm using this eight millimeter camera
to make a record of this place.

37:04.513 --> 37:05.681
To document it.

37:07.141 --> 37:08.726
To figure out what's going on.

37:12.980 --> 37:14.315
[man 1] Lots of fun here.

37:15.066 --> 37:16.692
There are no laws,

37:16.776 --> 37:19.320
so we can loot and kill as we please.

37:19.403 --> 37:21.113
[man 2] When I play the games,

37:21.197 --> 37:22.907
it's like, "I don't fuckin' care!"

37:22.990 --> 37:24.408
Total freedom. Oh yeah!

37:24.492 --> 37:25.576
[laughing]

37:25.660 --> 37:26.994
It feels pretty great.

37:29.580 --> 37:30.498
I hate it here.

37:31.082 --> 37:33.584
That's why I'm smoking weed…

37:33.668 --> 37:36.921
[giggling] …and just flipping out.

37:42.677 --> 37:45.554
[Kaito] It's been 26 days
since everyone disappeared.

37:46.055 --> 37:47.765
[panting]

37:49.558 --> 37:51.560
[running water]

37:57.066 --> 37:58.526
Hey, what are you doing?

38:00.778 --> 38:01.654
[Usagi] Ann?

38:10.079 --> 38:12.290
[Kaito] Excuse me, miss.
Is there something wrong?

38:15.501 --> 38:17.086
There are a lot more fish now.

38:17.169 --> 38:19.338
The plants
are starting to cover everything.

38:19.839 --> 38:21.966
It's like the further
we get from the city,

38:22.049 --> 38:24.176
the more that nature is growing rampant.

38:24.885 --> 38:26.929
[Kaito] Is that because
all the humans are gone?

38:27.013 --> 38:29.098
Well, sure, that's definitely part of it.

38:29.598 --> 38:32.059
But the plants have been growing
way too quickly.

38:33.644 --> 38:36.397
The people that are here
all came at different times.

38:36.480 --> 38:39.525
Certain things are rotting
more quickly than others.

38:39.608 --> 38:41.902
Time doesn't seem
to work the same way here.

38:45.448 --> 38:46.615
[Kaito] Where are you going?

38:49.285 --> 38:51.162
I'm going to try to get out of Tokyo.

38:52.121 --> 38:53.998
I wanna know what's behind all this.

39:01.255 --> 39:04.091
[Kaito] It's been 33 days
since everyone disappeared.

39:05.051 --> 39:07.011
I got a tip from a man I ran into.

39:08.346 --> 39:11.223
Apparently, there's a whole community
outside of Setagaya.

39:11.307 --> 39:12.850
I'm headed there right now.

39:21.525 --> 39:23.527
[laughter and chatter]

39:28.407 --> 39:30.910
[Kaito] Hi. I came here
because I heard a rumor

39:30.993 --> 39:33.913
about someone who has a memory
about what happened to us.

39:34.622 --> 39:36.248
Could you take me to them?

39:36.999 --> 39:38.334
Sure, it's just over here.

39:43.047 --> 39:45.132
[Kaito] Do you know
what it is they remember?

39:46.342 --> 39:49.345
Do you remember the day
you arrived in this world, huh?

39:50.096 --> 39:51.514
[Kaito] Yeah. I think so.

39:53.015 --> 39:54.850
Did you see something in the sky?

39:55.601 --> 39:58.020
- The fireworks?
- [Kaito] Fireworks?

39:59.647 --> 40:02.566
Yes, I remember. I saw them.

40:05.403 --> 40:06.779
Yeah, I saw them too.

40:08.739 --> 40:10.491
This way. Come on.

40:22.837 --> 40:26.298
This woman has a pretty crazy story
about them. Come on.

40:27.383 --> 40:28.968
She's there. Over there.

40:31.470 --> 40:34.557
This guy wants to hear
about the fireworks. Can you tell him?

40:36.600 --> 40:37.643
[woman] Huh?

40:38.477 --> 40:39.395
Oh.

40:40.479 --> 40:41.730
The fireworks.

40:46.610 --> 40:49.780
I have a story about them.
Would you like to hear it?

40:50.739 --> 40:51.740
[Kaito] Yes.

40:53.117 --> 40:54.535
[giggles]

40:54.618 --> 40:56.954
I must be the only one who remembers.

40:58.539 --> 40:59.582
[Kaito] Oh?

41:02.585 --> 41:04.128
When I was a little girl,

41:05.546 --> 41:07.381
I had a brain operation,

41:07.465 --> 41:10.050
so they drilled a hole, a little one,

41:10.134 --> 41:11.844
right here into my skull.

41:13.762 --> 41:15.306
Maybe that's the reason.

41:18.350 --> 41:19.727
I'm the only person

41:20.603 --> 41:23.314
who seems to remember
everything about that day.

41:25.816 --> 41:27.234
When…

41:27.985 --> 41:29.069
those…

41:29.570 --> 41:31.655
fireworks flew up into the sky…

41:34.450 --> 41:35.409
I saw them.

41:36.202 --> 41:37.328
They flashed,

41:38.204 --> 41:39.705
and they looked real.

41:41.457 --> 41:42.333
But…

41:43.667 --> 41:44.710
but…

41:46.378 --> 41:48.005
they weren't actually--

41:48.088 --> 41:49.548
- [gunshot]
- [gasps]

41:49.632 --> 41:51.342
[shouting and gunfire on film]

41:52.301 --> 41:54.136
- [Kaito panting]
- [burst of gunfire]

41:55.054 --> 41:57.848
- [man] It's the King of Spades!
- [gunfire continues]

42:00.100 --> 42:01.477
[Kaito grunting]

42:02.978 --> 42:04.980
[Kaito gasping]

42:13.197 --> 42:15.199
[panting]

42:18.619 --> 42:20.621
[hyperventilating]

42:31.590 --> 42:33.050
This documentary…

42:35.135 --> 42:37.721
is the only proof that I ever existed.

42:39.765 --> 42:42.810
I'll do whatever I can to keep it safe
until it's found.

42:45.771 --> 42:46.981
[groans]

42:55.155 --> 42:56.365
[Usagi gasps]

42:59.535 --> 43:01.203
[both breathing unsteadily]

43:05.916 --> 43:07.209
[gasps]

43:07.293 --> 43:09.336
[rattling]

43:09.420 --> 43:11.171
[rumbling]

43:11.255 --> 43:12.965
[caravan shaking]

43:13.048 --> 43:14.425
[crockery rattling]

43:15.134 --> 43:16.427
What's that sound?

43:17.803 --> 43:19.096
[gasps]

43:20.097 --> 43:22.099
[rumbling intensifying]

43:22.891 --> 43:25.102
[engine roaring]

43:28.063 --> 43:29.690
- [gunshot]
- [Usagi yelps]

43:30.441 --> 43:32.610
[gasps] Arisu, this way!

43:37.114 --> 43:39.325
- [gunshot]
- Watch out! That way!

43:55.716 --> 43:57.217
[gunfire continues]

44:01.138 --> 44:02.056
Usagi!

44:02.139 --> 44:03.682
- [gasping]
- [metal creaks]

44:13.984 --> 44:14.943
[Arisu] Hey!

44:16.570 --> 44:18.238
[burst of gunfire]

44:42.179 --> 44:43.389
[gasps]

44:45.933 --> 44:47.351
[explosion]

44:51.355 --> 44:53.357
- [heavy fire]
- [yelping]

44:55.943 --> 44:57.277
[choking]

45:14.920 --> 45:16.922
[rustling]

45:25.431 --> 45:27.516
[footsteps]

45:27.599 --> 45:28.642
Usagi?

45:33.230 --> 45:34.356
Who's there?

46:01.550 --> 46:03.260
Are you a citizen?

46:04.553 --> 46:05.679
Huh?

46:07.431 --> 46:08.807
[Arisu] I guess you're not.

46:11.602 --> 46:12.686
[winces]

46:13.937 --> 46:15.314
Why did you attack me?

46:16.732 --> 46:19.193
You woulda gotten killed
if you'd kept running like that.

46:21.236 --> 46:23.822
I told him to leave you behind.
We don't need dead weight.

46:25.199 --> 46:28.327
But guess what?
He wanted to carry you all the way here.

46:29.828 --> 46:30.871
Who did?

46:38.629 --> 46:41.131
You'd better thank him, Arisu.

46:42.925 --> 46:44.676
How do you know my name?

46:44.760 --> 46:46.553
That's what he called you.

46:51.934 --> 46:53.602
Oh, watch out.

46:54.520 --> 46:58.232
He's in a pretty foul mood
since you messed up our plan.

46:59.775 --> 47:00.651
[chuckles]

47:05.614 --> 47:07.616
[wind rustling through leaves]

47:43.443 --> 47:44.528
Aguni?

47:47.447 --> 47:48.657
Hey, newbie.

47:52.828 --> 47:54.663
[theme music]
